            <ArticleTitle>Infarction of extralobar pulmonary sequestration after blunt trauma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1127-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pulmonary sequestration is a rare congenital lung malformation that occurs in either an intralobar or extralobar location and is generally asymptomatic. We report an unusual case of a child who presented with infarction of a previously asymptomatic extralobar pulmonary sequestration after blunt trauma, eventually requiring surgical excision.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
